cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research package, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Cloitre recurrence research package"
abstract: >-
  An AI-assisted research package curated by the repository maintainer,
  containing proofs, computational certificates, and verification software
  concerning stabilization and attainable eventual increments in the
  recurrence b(n+1) = b(n) + (b(n) mod n). The universal stabilization
  conjecture remains open, and the principal new proofs await external
  mathematical review.
authors:
  - family-names: "Davis"
    given-names: "Justin"
    email: "Justin@Kodaxa.dev"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
version: 0.1.0-audit
date-released: "2026-07-28"
# No `commit:` field, deliberately. A file cannot contain the hash of the commit
# that contains it: writing one in changes the file, which changes the commit,
# so the recorded value is stale the moment it is committed. That is exactly how
# the `7ccda13` line on the paper's title page went stale, and it was removed
# for the same reason. Provenance is by tag instead -- tag the frozen commit,
# then record the tag in manuscript/arxiv/README.md, which a later commit can do
# without contradicting itself.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kodaxadev/cloitre-recurrence"
url: "https://github.com/Kodaxadev/cloitre-recurrence"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - integer recurrence
  - modular arithmetic
  - computational number theory
  - formal verification
  - research software
